# Alert Rule Monitoring 

Azure alert rules are policies customers can configure to be notified when they are approaching or exceeding their resource usage limits.  
This document provides a conceptual overview about alert rules and monitoring used in Azure quota. 

## Alert rules 

Azure quota alerts rules are mechanisms that are created and used by Azure customers to manage their cloud resources, such as storage capacity, and other indicators of performance and usage. 
Alert rules are created, by configuring specific usage scenarios such a set capacity usage of 80%, with frequency of checking every 15 minutes, and conditions of firing a severity-level alert when this occurs.
When a customer's usage of a particular resource exceeds or approaches the defined threshold, an alert is generated, based on the defined parameters to indicate that the customer is nearing their quota limit.

## Monitor alert rules 

Azure alert rule monitoring typically works by using automated monitoring tools and services that track usage metrics and thresholds specified in the alert rules, set by the customer. These metrics can include resource consumption, error rates, and other indicators of performance and usage.
When a metric reaches the threshold defined in an alert rule, such as 80% usage capacity, the monitoring system triggers an alert, which is then sent to the appropriate individuals or teams for action. The alert can be delivered by email, SMS, or via a mobile app push with details about the metrics that triggered the alert.
Monitoring can be done in real-time, with alerts being sent out within seconds of a threshold and are available on the Azure quota dashboard.  
Overall, Azure quota alert rule monitoring is essential to manage cloud infrastructure, and provides customers with timely alerts and insights into usage trends and anomalies, which allows them to take proactive steps to optimize their resources and avoid or resolve potential issues. 
For more information access the Azure Portal and follow the UI/UX or review How to create alert rules how-to documentation. 

